<hr data-start="1746" data-end="1749">
<h1 data-start="1751" data-end="1805">🟨 4. <strong data-start="1759" data-end="1803">Método-V para primos gemelos (Twin Test)</strong></h1>
<p data-start="1806" data-end="1859"><strong data-start="1806" data-end="1858">ESTÁ MEDIO HECHO — falta formalizar como teorema</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1861" data-end="1941">Sí, el <strong data-start="1868" data-end="1901">método-V está en tu documento</strong>, pero <strong data-start="1908" data-end="1938">no lo hemos convertido aún</strong> a:</p>
<ul data-start="1943" data-end="2004">
<li data-start="1943" data-end="1960">
<p data-start="1945" data-end="1960">teorema formal,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1961" data-end="1977">
<p data-start="1963" data-end="1977">implicaciones,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1978" data-end="2004">
<p data-start="1980" data-end="2004">pseudocódigo finalizado.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2006" data-end="2030">El método-V consiste en:</p>
<ul data-start="2032" data-end="2245">
<li data-start="2032" data-end="2056">
<p data-start="2034" data-end="2056">Tomar un número <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2057" data-end="2077">
<p data-start="2059" data-end="2077">ver residuo mod 6,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2078" data-end="2122">
<p data-start="2080" data-end="2122">formar la pareja candidata <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6k-1, 6k+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2123" data-end="2158">
<p data-start="2125" data-end="2158">aplicar cribas modulares rápidas,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2159" data-end="2210">
<p data-start="2161" data-end="2210">usar <strong data-start="2166" data-end="2188">test V de simetría</strong> para descartar pares,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2211" data-end="2245">
<p data-start="2213" data-end="2245">y quedarte sólo con los gemelos.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2247" data-end="2368">Tu método-V es básicamente un <strong data-start="2277" data-end="2318">test determinista-modular/acumulativo</strong> para decidir si <code data-start="2335" data-end="2345">(n, n+2)</code> sobreviven las cribas.</p>
<hr data-start="2370" data-end="2373">
<h1 data-start="2375" data-end="2441">👉 <strong data-start="2380" data-end="2394">SI QUIERES</strong> puedo convertir AHORA MISMO el <strong data-start="2426" data-end="2438">Método-V</strong> a:</h1>
<h2 data-start="2443" data-end="2512">🔵 <strong data-start="2449" data-end="2510">(A) Teorema de primos gemelos por Método-V (forma lógica)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2513" data-end="2518">tipo:</p>
