, haciendo explícitas las familias modulares, la garantía “hay al menos un miembro”, la condición que fuerza la aparición de un primo que impide cierta factorización, y la cadena de implicaciones <code data-start="308" data-end="320">v ⇒ V ⇒ v'</code> con sus consecuencias. No voy a pedir aclaraciones: haré una interpretación razonable y útil del texto (si algo no es lo que querías, lo puedo ajustar luego).</p>
<p data-start="481" data-end="513">Voy a entregarlo en tres partes:</p>
<ol data-start="515" data-end="800">
<li data-start="515" data-end="605">
<p data-start="518" data-end="605"><strong data-start="518" data-end="577">Definición del método y familias modulares (matemática)</strong> — teorema/esquema lógico.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="606" data-end="672">
<p data-start="609" data-end="672"><strong data-start="609" data-end="669">Cadena de implicaciones (v ⇒ V ⇒ v′) y su interpretación</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="673" data-end="800">
<p data-start="676" data-end="800"><strong data-start="676" data-end="724">Pseudocódigo ejecutable (estilo verificable)</strong> que genera familias, aplica el test-V y produce miembros (con comentarios).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="802" data-end="805">
<h1 data-start="807" data-end="871">1) Método-V — Marco matemático y teoremización (pseudoteorema)</h1>
<p data-start="873" data-end="1158"><strong data-start="873" data-end="886">Objetivo:</strong> construir familias aritméticas infinitas <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span></span></span></span> tal que cada familia contiene al menos un entero <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> que <strong data-start="1005" data-end="1023">pasa el Test-V</strong> (es decir, sobrevive a las obstrucciones modulares/ factorales) y — en muchos casos — produce un primo o una pareja de primos gemelos.</p>
<h2 data-start="1160" data-end="1175">Definiciones</h2>
<ul data-start="1177" data-end="2219">
<li data-start="1177" data-end="1262">
<p data-start="1179" data-end="1262">Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span></span></span></span> un conjunto finito de primos pequeños (p. ej. <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2,3,5,\dots,p_k\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1263" data-end="1383">
<p data-start="1265" data-end="1383">Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M = 6 \cdot \prod_{p\in P} p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1858em; vertical-align: -0.4358em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol small-op" style="position: relative; top: 0em;">∏</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1786em;"><span style="top: -2.4003em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="mrel mtight">∈</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.4358em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span> (o cualquier módulo conveniente que incluya 6 para respetar clases <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6k\pm1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">±</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1384" data-end="1569">
<p data-start="1386" data-end="1569">Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span> un subconjunto de residuos módulo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span> elegidos para <em data-start="1450" data-end="1458">evitar</em> las familias fácilmente factorizables (por ejemplo residuos que producirían factores tipo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6a-1)(6b+1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal">a</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal">b</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1570" data-end="1780">
<p data-start="1572" data-end="1699">Para cada elección de parámetros (p. ej. un primo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> usado para fijar una obstrucción), definimos una <strong data-start="1677" data-end="1688">familia</strong> aritmética</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">N</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>r</mi><mspace></mspace><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{M,r} := \{\, n \in \mathbb{N} : n \equiv r \pmod M\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0993em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4637em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mclose">}</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
</li>
<li data-start="1782" data-end="1944">
<p data-start="1784" data-end="1944"><strong data-start="1784" data-end="1802">Predicado v(n)</strong>: condiciones locales/computacionales mínimas (p. ej. pasa cribas por los primeros t primos, resiste las formas triviales de factorización).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1945" data-end="2082">
<p data-start="1947" data-end="2082"><strong data-start="1947" data-end="1965">Predicado V(n)</strong>: versión reforzada de v — pasa Test-V completo (memorias, patrones de residuos, chequeos de productos acumulados).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2083" data-end="2219">
<p data-start="2085" data-end="2219"><strong data-start="2085" data-end="2104">Predicado v'(n)</strong>: versión aún más fuerte (p. ej. además <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> no tiene factores pequeños, o alguna congruencia adversa forzada).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="2221" data-end="2247">Pseudoteorema (esquema)</h2>
<p data-start="2249" data-end="2530"><strong data-start="2249" data-end="2280">Teorema (esquema Método-V).</strong><br data-start="2280" data-end="2283">
Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span> y una familia <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{M,r}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0993em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> construida por condiciones modulares que evitan las formas factorizables (especificadas por el método). Si las condiciones modulares son compatibles (por el TCR) y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span> es coprimo con <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span></span></span></span>, entonces:</p>
<ol data-start="2532" data-end="3408">
<li data-start="2532" data-end="2602">
<p data-start="2535" data-end="2602"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{M,r}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0993em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> es infinita (es una progresión aritmética).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2603" data-end="2897">
<p data-start="2606" data-end="2897">Si en la construcción elegimos un primo auxiliar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> que hace <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace></mspace><mspace width="0.4444em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n+1\equiv0\pmod q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.4444em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> para todos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>r</mi><mspace></mspace><mspace width="0.4444em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\equiv r\pmod M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4637em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.4444em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, entonces <strong data-start="2735" data-end="2771">cada miembro de la familia tiene</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> divisible por <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> (lo que puede forzar compuestos o, si controlamos residuos, bloquear ciertas factorizaciones).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2898" data-end="3136">
<p data-start="2901" data-end="3136">Entre las <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{M,r}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0993em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mpunct mtight">,</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> para distintos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> existe al menos una que contiene un <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> tal que <code data-start="3004" data-end="3010">v(n)</code> es verdadero (o <code data-start="3027" data-end="3033">V(n)</code>) — esto se asegura construyendo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span></span></span></span> para evitar los residuos que generan L3/L4 en el esquema Sofí.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3137" data-end="3408">
<p data-start="3140" data-end="3408">En particular, el método genera <strong data-start="3172" data-end="3194">familias infinitas</strong> y — por Dirichlet si hace falta añadir una condición coprima para primes buscados— <strong data-start="3278" data-end="3331">cada familia contiene infinitos primos candidatos</strong> o al menos infinitos miembros que no cumplen las factorizaciones prohibidas.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="3410" data-end="3814"><strong data-start="3410" data-end="3438">Interpretación práctica:</strong> escogiendo condiciones modulares (usando CRT) puedes “fabricar” clases <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace></mspace><mspace width="0.4444em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\pmod M</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">r</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.4444em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> que <strong data-start="3527" data-end="3537">evitan</strong> los residuos que provocarían factorizaciones de tipo L3/L4; como consecuencia obtienes familias infinitas con miembros que sobreviven a las cribas elementales — y entre esos miembros, por densidad/Dirichlet, hay muchos candidatos primos o semiprimos con la estructura buscada.</p>
<hr data-start="3816" data-end="3819">
<h1 data-start="3821" data-end="3879">2) Cadena de implicaciones <code data-start="3850" data-end="3862">v ⇒ V ⇒ v'</code> y su significado</h1>
<p data-start="3881" data-end="3935">Expresado en implicaciones lógicas (modo que pediste):</p>
