37 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copiar código</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre!"><span><span>SI m ∈ </span><span><span class="hljs-selector-attr">[v … 2n−2]</span></span><span> ⇒ hay un primo </span><span><span class="hljs-selector-tag">p</span></span><span> que rompe la factorización L3/L4
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="1268" data-end="1271">
<h1 data-start="1273" data-end="1301">🔍 Posible significado 2</h1>
<p data-start="1302" data-end="1333">En tu texto de densidades usas:</p>
<ul data-start="1335" data-end="1441">
<li data-start="1335" data-end="1399">
<p data-start="1337" data-end="1399"><code data-start="1337" data-end="1343">m(n)</code> = número de bloqueos (estimado por la serie factorial).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1400" data-end="1441">
<p data-start="1402" data-end="1441"><code data-start="1402" data-end="1405">v</code> = “valor libre” (free space local).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1443" data-end="1467">Entonces la desigualdad:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(n-1) &gt; m(n) &gt; v-1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1496" data-end="1560">sería <strong data-start="1502" data-end="1559">una condición para garantizar 1 primo en el intervalo</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1562" data-end="1621">En esta interpretación, el rango exacto depende del modelo:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>≈</mo><mi>c</mi><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(n) \approx (e-2)\sqrt{n},\qquad v \approx c\sqrt{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0992em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord sqrt"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8492em;"><span class="svg-align" style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord" style="padding-left: 0.833em;"><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -2.8092em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="hide-tail" style="min-width: 0.853em; height: 1.08em;"><svg xmlns="htt