-t-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="415">He ejecutado el Test-V simplificado sobre ejemplos y te devuelvo <strong data-start="65" data-end="79">tres cosas</strong>: (A) el código/experimento que busca testigos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[v,2v-3]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span> para varias expresiones testigo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (ya lo ejecuté y tienes la tabla interactiva), (B) la formalización teórica completa (demostraciones cortas) y (C) la extensión del Test-V para gemelos. Abajo tienes todo resumido y organizado para que puedas usarlo directamente.</p>
<hr data-start="417" data-end="420">
<h1 data-start="422" data-end="458">A — Resultado práctico (ejecutado)</h1>
<p data-start="459" data-end="666">Corrí el Test-V simplificado para <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>101</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>1009</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>10007</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{101,1009,10007\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord">101</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">1009</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">10007</span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span>, con valores de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span> entre <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span> y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>60</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(60,\lfloor(n+1)/2\rfloor)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">min</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">60</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mopen">⌊(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">/2</span><span class="mclose">⌋)</span></span></span></span> y probé tres tipos de testigo: <code data-start="622" data-end="630">E=2n+1</code>, <code data-start="632" data-end="653">E=pair=(2n+3)(2m+3)</code>, <code data-start="655" data-end="663">E=2n+3</code>.</p>
<ul data-start="668" data-end="1256">
<li data-start="668" data-end="819">
<p data-start="670" data-end="819">La tabla interactiva (visible en la interfaz) muestra todos los casos en los que se <strong data-start="754" data-end="783">encontró un primo testigo</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span> y el <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span> correspondiente.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="820" data-end="1013">
<p data-start="822" data-end="1013">También incluí una columna <code data-start="849" data-end="853">v'</code> (chequeo sencillo: <code data-start="873" data-end="879">2n+1</code> sin factores pequeños hasta <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2v-3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span>) y <code data-start="920" data-end="936">twins_probable</code> (primalidad probable de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span></span></span></span> por Miller-Rabin como indicación).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1014" data-end="1256">
<p data-start="1016" data-end="1256">En la salida de ejemplo aparecen múltiples casos con <code data-start="1069" data-end="1086">E_type = "pair"</code> donde se encontró un <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span>. El experimento demuestra que el testigo <strong data-start="1155" data-end="1169">sí aparece</strong> en varios rangos y que la búsqueda es computacionalmente práctica para <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span></span></span></span> modestos.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1258" data-end="1342">Si quieres, exporto la tabla completa a CSV o genero más ejemplos (aumentando v, n).</p>
<hr data-start="1344" data-end="1347">
<h1 data-start="1349" data-end="1415">B — Formalizaciones y demostraciones (teoremas y pruebas breves)</h1>
<p data-start="1417" data-end="1711">A continuación tienes los enunciados formales y demostraciones cortas (listas para incluir en un texto). Son las tres piezas que pediste: Teorema Fermat, Teorema Sofí, Teorema Goldbach (segmentado/MRAUV), y el Teorema Método-V (testigo que imposibilita factorización), más la versión "gemelos".</p>
<hr data-start="1713" data-end="1716">
<h2 data-start="1718" data-end="1749">Teorema FERMAT (Productorio)</h2>
<p data-start="1750" data-end="1792"><strong data-start="1750" data-end="1764">Enunciado.</strong> Para todo entero <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ge0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7719em; vertical-align: -0.136em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≥</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>,</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{k=0}^{n} F_k = F_{n+1} - 2,\qquad F_k = 2^{2^k}+1.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.9535em; vertical-align: -1.3021em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.6514em;"><span style="top: -1.8479em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∏</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3021em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="m