</li>
<li data-start="7087" data-end="7337">
<p data-start="7089" data-end="7337">Si no se encuentra <code data-start="7108" data-end="7111">p</code> en primes_dividing_V con <code data-start="7137" data-end="7153">p&lt;=prime_bound</code>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span> puede tener factores primos grandes; entonces conviene usar <code data-start="7221" data-end="7255">g = gcd(V, any_candidate_number)</code> o aplicar factoring parcial (Pollard rho) para obtener factores grandes de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
