4237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copiar código</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-python"><span><span><span class="hljs-string">"""
test_mequation.py
Prueba de "conexión nula" (MEcuation) por bootstrap + SVD.
Incluye propuesta automática de hasta add_k nuevas observaciones
con estrategias: ortogonal a PC, casos límite y reducción de incertidumbre.
"""</span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> math, random
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> numpy </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> np
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> numpy.linalg </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> svd
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> math </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> log, exp

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># ---------- utilidades ----------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">build_feature_vector</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">E</span></span><span>):
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># features: [log(E), log(sqrt(E)), residual log - 2*log(sqrt)]</span></span><span>
    f1 = math.log(E)
    f2 = math.log(math.sqrt(E))
    f3 = f1 - </span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.0</span></span><span>*f2
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> np.array([f1, f2, f3], dtype=</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">float</span></span><span>)

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">center_columns</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">Y</span></span><span>):
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Y: x by d</span></span><span>
    col_mean = np.mean(Y, axis=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> Y - col_mean

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">propose_new_observations</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">observations, epsilons, k=<span class="hljs-number">4</span></span></span><span>):
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Three strategies combined:</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># 1) orthogonal to PC (approx): choose E with log near mean +/- gap</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># 2) extremes: push to extremes of existing intervals</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># 3) reduce uncertainty: same E but smaller eps</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Return list of tuples (E_val, eps_vector)</span></span><span>
    Ys = np.array([build_feature_vector(E) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> observations])
    Yc = center_columns(Ys)
    U,S,Vt = svd(Yc, full_matrices=</span><span><span class="hljs-literal">False</span></span><span>)
    pc1 = Vt[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> Vt.shape[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>]&gt;</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">else</span></span><span> np.zeros(Yc.shape[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>])
    mean_vec = np.mean(Ys, axis=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>)

    candidates=[]
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Strategy A: orthogonal perturbation in log-space</span></span><span>
    ort = np.zeros_like(mean_vec)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># choose direction roughly orthogonal to pc1</span></span><span>
    ort_dir = np.random.normal(size=mean_vec.shape)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># make orthogonal</span></span><span>
    ort_dir = ort_dir - (ort_dir.dot(pc1))*pc1
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> np.linalg.norm(ort_dir) == </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>:
        ort_dir = np.random.normal(size=mean_vec.shape)
    ort_dir = ort_dir / np.linalg.norm(ort_dir)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># map back to E via exponent on first component (log E)</span></span><span>
    delta_log = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.25</span></span><span>  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># step in log-space</span></span><span>
    new_log = mean_vec[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>] + delta_log * ort_dir[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>]
    E_ort = math.exp(new_log)
    candidates.append( (E_ort, [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.1</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.05</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.02</span></span><span>]) )

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Strategy B: extremes - push around current intervals</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># pick max and min observed log(E)</span></span><span>
    logs = [math.log(E) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> observations]
    minlog, maxlog = </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">min</span></span><span>(logs), </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">max</span></span><span>(logs)
    candidates.append( (math.exp(minlog - </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.3</span></span><span>), [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.1</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.05</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.02</span></span><span>]) )
    candidates.append( (math.exp(maxlog + </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.3</span></span><span>), [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.1</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.05</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.02</span></span><span>]) )

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># Strategy C: reduce uncertainty on a chosen observation (copy of first with smaller eps)</span></span><span>
    candidates.append( (observations[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>], [e*</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.3</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> e </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> epsilons[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>]]) )

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># return up to k</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> candidates[:k]

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># ---------- test function ----------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">test_connection_null</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">observations, epsilons, tau=<span class="hljs-number">1e-6</span></span></span><span>, bootstrap_N=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">300</span></span><span>, consensus=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.95</span></span><span>):
    x=</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span><span>(observations)
    d = </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span><span>(build_feature_vector(observations[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>]))
    deg_count = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> s </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">range</span></span><span>(bootstrap_N):
        Ys = np.zeros((x,d))
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">range</span></span><span>(x):
            base = build_feature_vector(observations[i])
            samp = np.array([ base[j] + random.uniform(-epsilons[i][j], epsilons[i][j]) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> j </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">range</span></span><span>(d) ])
            Ys[i,:] = samp
        Yc = center_columns(Ys)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">try</span></span><span>:
            S = svd(Yc, compute_uv=</span><span><span class="hljs-literal">False</span></span><span>)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">except</span></span><span> Exception:
            S = np.linalg.svd(Yc, compute_uv=</span><span><span class="hljs-literal">False</span></span><span>)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span><span>(S) == </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>:
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">continue</span></span><span>
        kappa = S[-</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>] / (S[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> S[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>] != </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">else</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-number">1e-30</span></span><span>)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> kappa &lt; tau:
            deg_count += </span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>
    deg_frac = deg_count / bootstrap_N
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> deg_frac

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># ---------- main flow ----------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> __name__ == </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"__main__"</span></span><span>:
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># --- INITIAL OBSERVATIONS (your 3 logs example) ---</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># E = 25, 49, 121 with given epsilons in log-space mapped to feature eps</span></span><span>
    obs = [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">25.0</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">49.0</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">121.0</span></span><span>]
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># epsilon vector per feature -- these are in log-units for f1, scaled for f2,f3</span></span><span>
    eps_examples = [
        [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.4</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.4</span></span><span>/</span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.0</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.01</span></span><span>],  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># for E=25</span></span><span>
        [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.44</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.44</span></span><span>/</span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.0</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.01</span></span><span>],
        [</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.444</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.444</span></span><span>/</span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.0</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.01</span></span><span>]
    ]

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># parameters</span></span><span>
    tau = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">1e-6</span></span><span>
    bootstrap_N = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">300</span></span><span>
    consensus = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.95</span></span><span>
    max_x = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">20</span></span><span>
    add_k = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">4</span></span><span>

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># iterative loop</span></span><span>
    observations = </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">list</span></span><span>(obs)
    epsilons = </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">list</span></span><span>(eps_examples)
    round_idx = </span><span><span class="hljs-number">0</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">while</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-literal">True</span></span><span>:
        round_idx += </span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>
        </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">f"Round <span class="hljs-subst">{round_idx}</span></span></span><span>: testing with x=</span><span><span class="hljs-subst">{<span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span></span><span>(observations)} observations ...")
        deg_frac = test_connection_null(observations, epsilons, tau=tau, bootstrap_N=bootstrap_N, consensus=consensus)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">f"  deg_frac = <span class="hljs-subst">{deg_frac:<span class="hljs-number">.4</span></span></span></span><span>f}")
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> deg_frac &gt;= consensus:
            </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"&gt;&gt;&gt; COLLAPSE detected: MEcuation exists within model (robust). STOP."</span></span><span>)
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">break</span></span><span>
        </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># stopping criteria</span></span><span>
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span><span>(observations) &gt;= max_x:
            </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"&gt;&gt;&gt; MAX_X reached and no collapse: conclude NO MEcuation (within this model). STOP."</span></span><span>)
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">break</span></span><span>
        </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># propose new observations (guided)</span></span><span>
        new_cand = propose_new_observations(observations, epsilons, k=add_k)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">f"  proposing <span class="hljs-subst">{<span class="hljs-built_in">len</span></span></span></span><span>(new_cand)} new observations ...")
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> Enew, eps_new </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> new_cand:
            observations.append(Enew)
            epsilons.append(eps_new)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># loop continues</span></span><span>

    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment"># print final observation set</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Final observations (log values):"</span></span><span>)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> i,E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">enumerate</span></span><span>(observations):
        </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span></span><span>(i+</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>, E, math.log(E))
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="5590" data-end="5602"><strong data-start="5590" data-end="5600">Notas:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="5603" data-end="5837">
<li data-start="5603" data-end="5705">
<p data-start="5605" data-end="5705">Las <code data-start="5609" data-end="5619">epsilons</code> son vectores por feature. Ajusta si tus incertidumbres reales están en otra escala.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5706" data-end="5837">
<p data-start="5708" data-end="5837">El generador <code data-start="5721" data-end="5747">propose_new_observations</code> incluye la estrategia “ortogonal + extremos + reducción de incertidumbre” que dije antes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="5839" data-end="5842">
<h1 data-start="5844" data-end="5910">B — Cuatro propuestas concretas (numéricas) para añadir ya a <code data-start="5907" data-end="5910">x</code></h1>
<p data-start="5912" data-end="6011">Partiendo de tus tres originales <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>25</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>49</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>121</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\{25,49,121\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord">25</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">49</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">121</span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> — sus logs están en (≈3.2189, 3.8918, 4.7958).</p>
<p data-start="6013" data-end="6117">Para <strong data-start="6018" data-end="6041">probar la hipótesis</strong> (intentar forzar colapso o mostrar que no existe), añade <strong data-start="6099" data-end="6116">estos 4 casos</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="6119" data-end="6545">
<li data-start="6119" data-end="6228">
<p data-start="6122" data-end="6228"><strong data-start="6122" data-end="6133">E4 = 33</strong> — <code data-start="6136" data-end="6152">log ≈ 3.496504</code><br data-start="6152" data-end="6155">
→ cae en la intersección entre I1 e I2; es útil para ver convergencia.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6230" data-end="6319">
<p data-start="6233" data-end="6319"><strong data-start="6233" data-end="6244">E5 = 55</strong> — <code data-start="6247" data-end="6263">log ≈ 4.007333</code><br data-start="6263" data-end="6266">
→ cae entre I2 y el centro; ayuda a llenar huecos.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6321" data-end="6428">
<p data-start="6324" data-end="6428"><strong data-start="6324" data-end="6335">E6 = 98</strong> — <code data-start="6338" data-end="6351">log ≈ 4.585</code><br data-start="6351" data-end="6354">
→ situado entre I2 superior y I3 inferior; mueve la masa hacia el alto.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6430" data-end="6545">
<p data-start="6433" data-end="6545"><strong data-start="6433" data-end="6444">E7 = 16</strong> — <code data-start="6447" data-end="6463">log ≈ 2.772588</code><br data-start="6463" data-end="6466">
→ extremo inferior para comprobar si la dimensión requiere rango más amplio.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="6547" data-end="6769">Asigna incertidumbres (ejemplo) similares a las tuyas: for each E_i use <code data-start="6619" data-end="6647">[eps_log, eps_log/2, 0.01]</code> with <code data-start="6653" data-end="6662">eps_log</code> ~ 0.4 (or smaller if you can measure better). These are exactly the kind of <code data-start="6739" data-end="6749">epsilons</code> the script expects.</p>
