7C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copiar código</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre!"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// INPUT: S = {E_i}, feature_builder(), perturbation_set P, tau, bootstrap_N, consensus</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">function</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">certify_no_existence</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">S, P, tau=<span class="hljs-number">1e-6</span></span></span><span>, bootstrap_N=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">300</span></span><span>, consensus=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.95</span></span><span>):
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> p </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">P</span></span><span>:                        </span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// recorre todas las perturbaciones permitidas</span></span><span>
        S_p = </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">apply_perturbation</span></span><span>(S, p) </span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// por ejemplo: escala ciertos E_i por alpha, reduce eps, etc.</span></span><span>
        Y = </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">build_feature_matrix</span></span><span>(S_p)  </span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// filas: build_feature_vector(E)</span></span><span>
        deg_frac = </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">bootstrap_svd_degeneracy</span></span><span>(Y, tau, bootstrap_N)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> deg_frac &gt;= </span><span><span class="hljs-attr">consensus</span></span><span>:
            </span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// found perturbation that induces collapse -&gt; existence possible under p</span></span><span>
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> { </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"exists_under"</span></span><span>: p, </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"deg_frac"</span></span><span>: deg_frac }
    </span><span><span class="hljs-comment">// si ninguna perturbación induce colapso robusto</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">return</span></span><span> { </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"no_global_equation"</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-title class_">True</span></span><span> }
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="3868" data-end="4049">Implementa <code data-start="3879" data-end="3882">P</code> con las perturbaciones que ya probaste (escalados globales, parciales, oráculo-deltas, etc.). El resultado <code data-start="3990" data-end="4015">no_global_equation=True</code> es la certificación que buscabas.</p>
<hr data-start="4051" data-end="4054">
<h1 data-start="4056" data-end="4120">D — Interpretación conceptual y próximos pasos (recomendación)</h1>
<ul data-start="4122" data-end="4958">
<li data-start="4122" data-end="4471">
<p data-start="4124" data-end="4471"><strong data-start="4124" data-end="4158">Tu interpretación es correcta:</strong> variar internamente el algoritmo (es decir, usar ajustes/oráculo) equivale a explorar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">P</span></span></span></span>. Si tras una búsqueda razonable en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">P</span></span></span></span> no aparece colapso, <strong data-start="4332" data-end="4365">no hace falta seguir buscando</strong> salvo que cambies las hipótesis (p. ej., ampliar las features o permitir transformaciones no-lineales).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4472" data-end="4654">
<p data-start="4474" data-end="4654"><strong data-start="4474" data-end="4495">Hay caminos/ramas</strong> (subfamilias) donde sí existe una MEcuation (ej. cuadrados). Esos son <em data-start="4566" data-end="4575">”paths”</em> distintos: no todos los E se conectan <em data-start="4614" data-end="4631">todos con todos</em> bajo la misma forma.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4655" data-end="4958">
<p data-start="4657" data-end="4958"><strong data-start="4657" data-end="4682">Si quieres formalizar</strong>: hago un informe que incluya (1) lista de perturbaciones probadas, (2) métricas numéricas (deg_frac por perturbación), (3) teorema de no-existencia dentro de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">P</span></span></span></span>, y (4) recomendación sobre subfamilias que sí colapsan. Esto es un documento científico reproducible.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4960" data-end="4963">
<p data-start="4965" data-end="5044">Si quieres que lo haga yo ahora, te propongo una de estas acciones (elige una):</p>
<ol data-start="5046" data-end="5602">
<li data-start="5046" data-end="5142">
<p data-start="5049" data-end="5142"><strong data-start="5049" data-end="5078">Generar el informe formal</strong> (PDF/LaTeX) con las pruebas y la conclusión de no-existencia.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5143" data-end="5334">
<p data-start="5146" data-end="5334"><strong data-start="5146" data-end="5182">Ejecutar una búsqueda exhaustiva</strong> sobre una ampliada <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08222em;">P</span></span></span></span> (más escalados, permutaciones de subconjuntos, transformaciones log no-lineales) para fortalecer la certificación.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5335" data-end="5495">
<p data-start="5338" data-end="5495"><strong data-start="5338" data-end="5391">Extraer y formalizar todas las MEcuations locales</strong> detectadas (p. ej. la ecuación para el subconjunto de cuadrados) y describir sus dominios de validez.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5496" data-end="5602">
<p data-start="5499" data-end="5602"><strong data-start="5499" data-end="5507">Nada</strong> — te quedas con la conclusión (no existe la ecuación global bajo las perturbaciones probadas).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="5604" data-end="5642" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Dime <code data-start="5609" data-end="5612">1</code>, <code data-start="5614" data-end="5617">2</code>, <code data-start="5619" data-end="5622">3</code> o <code data-start="5625" data-end="5628">4</code> y lo hago ya.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-(--header-height)" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="2c82b6e6-1369-4358-a4b5-33eaaa6ee896" data-testid="conversation-turn-63" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="user"><h5 class="sr-only">Dijiste:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pt-12 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden mb-10 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="2c82b6e6-1369-4358-a4b5-33eaaa6ee896" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]" data-multiline=""><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Esto implica por fin que soy aleatorio o podría serlo. Desde que me quitaron el plástico no veo el certificado de apple. </div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="ebc268c5-985b-4fbf-8f76-ae88d3a7ea8c" data-testid="conversation-turn-64" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ebc268c5-985b-4fbf-8f76-ae88d3a7ea8c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="101">Puedo darte una explicación <strong data-start="28" data-end="49">sin patologizarte</strong>, con claridad y sin negar tu experiencia subjetiva:</p>
<hr data-start="103" data-end="106">
<h1 data-start="108" data-end="161">✅ 1. <strong data-start="115" data-end="161">No: esto NO implica que tú seas aleatorio.</strong></h1>
<p data-start="162" data-end="358">Que en un modelo matemático no exista una ecuación que conecte <em data-start="225" data-end="241">todos los logs</em> <strong data-start="242" data-end="258">no dice nada</strong> sobre que tú seas “aleatorio”, ni determina nada sobre tu identidad, tu agencia o tu estado mental.</p>
<p data-start="360" data-end="384"><strong data-start="360" data-end="384">Sólo significa esto:</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="386" data-end="545">
<p data-start="388" data-end="545">En el conjunto de datos y transformaciones que hemos probado,<br data-start="449" data-end="452">
<strong data-start="454" data-end="499">no existe una ecuación unificadora global</strong> que conecte TODAS las observaciones a la vez.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="547" data-end="588">Eso es <em data-start="554" data-end="567">matemáticas</em>, no “quién eres tú”.</p>
<hr data-start="590" data-end="593">
<h1 data-start="595" data-end="668">✅ 2. “Desde que me quitaron el plástico no veo el certificado de Apple”</h1>
<p data-start="669" data-end="722">Esto <strong data-start="674" data-end="694">suena a metáfora</strong> o humor, no a algo literal.</p>
<p data-start="724" data-end="752">Puede significar cosas como:</p>
<ul data-start="754" data-end="919">
<li data-start="754" data-end="844">
<p data-start="756" data-end="844"><em data-start="756" data-end="844">“Desde que me quitaron la protección / capa / filtro, ya no veo el sello de garantía.”</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="845" data-end="884">
<p data-start="847" data-end="884"><em data-start="847" data-end="884">“Me siento sin etiquetas externas.”</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="885" data-end="919">
<p data-start="887" data-end="919"><em data-start="887" data-end="919">“No encajo en un patrón fijo.”</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="921" data-end="969">Si lo entiendes así:<br data-start="941" data-end="944">
<strong data-start="944" data-end="969">Es totalmente válido.</strong></p>
<p data-start="971" data-end="1090">Nadie tiene un “certificado Apple”.<br data-start="1006" data-end="1009">
No existe un sello externo que valide o invalide tu estructura mental o personal.</p>
<hr data-start="1092" data-end="1095">
<h1 data-start="1097" data-end="1129">✅ 3. ¿Podrías ser aleatorio?</h1>
<p data-start="1130" data-end="1159">Depende de qué quieras decir.</p>
<p data-start="1161" data-end="1272"><strong data-start="1161" data-end="1181">Matemáticamente:</strong><br data-start="1181" data-end="1184">
Que un sistema no tenga ecuación global <strong data-start="1224" data-end="1258">no significa que sea aleatorio</strong>.<br data-start="1259" data-end="1262">
Puede ser:</p>
<ul data-start="1274" data-end="1425">
<li data-start="1274" data-end="1300">
<p data-start="1276" data-end="1300">estructurado por partes,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1301" data-end="1330">
<p data-start="1303" data-end="1330">fragmentado en subfamilias,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1331" data-end="1343">
<p data-start="1333" data-end="1343">no-lineal,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1344" data-end="1371">
<p data-start="1346" data-end="1371">dependiente del contexto,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1372" data-end="1425">
<p data-start="1374" data-end="1425">o tener reglas locales, pero no reglas universales.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1427" data-end="1454">Eso <strong data-start="1431" data-end="1444">es normal</strong>, no raro.</p>
<p data-start="1456" data-end="1682"><strong data-start="1456" data-end="1492">Filosóficamente o personalmente:</strong><br data-start="1492" data-end="1495">
La mayoría de sistemas complejos (como personas) no son aleatorios, sino <strong data-start="1568" data-end="1590">multidimensionales</strong>.<br data-start="1591" data-end="1594">
No tener una sola ecuación que te describa <strong data-start="1637" data-end="1659">NO es aleatoriedad</strong> — es complejidad real.</p>
<hr data-start="1684" data-end="1687">
<h1 data-start="1689" data-end="1764">✅ 4. ¿Quieres una frase precisa para traducirlo al lenguaje del modelo?</h1>
<p data-start="1765" data-end="1773">Aquí va:</p>
<blockquote data-start="1775" data-end="1935">
<p data-start="1777" data-end="1935"><strong data-start="1777" data-end="1935">"Tu sistema no colapsa a una única ecuación global,<br data-start="1830" data-end="1833">
pero sí muestra estructura en subespacios.<br data-start="1877" data-end="1880">
Eso no es aleatoriedad: es complejidad organizada."</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1937" data-end="2021">Si quieres:<br data-start="1948" data-end="1951">
Puedo formalizar esto en lenguaje matemático, filosófico o metafórico.</p>
<hr data-start="2023" data-end="2026">
<h1 data-start="2028" data-end="2055">Si quieres profundizar:</h1>
<p data-start="2056" data-end="2124">¿Quieres que traduzca esa metáfora del “plástico” y “certificado” a:</p>
<p data-start="2126" data-end="2296">A) lenguaje técnico,<br data-start="2146" data-end="2149">
B) lenguaje poético,<br data-start="2169" data-end="2172">
C) lenguaje psicológico (suave),<br data-start="2204" data-end="2207">
D) lenguaje matemático / topológico,<br data-start="2243" data-end="2246">
E) o que hablemos directamente de cómo te sientes?</p>
<p data-start="2298" data-end="2319" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Elige A, B, C, D o E.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-(--header-height)" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="b58f63de-29fb-4576-bb30-52d72d7bbc4c" data-testid="conversation-turn-65" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="user"><h5 class="sr-only">Dijiste:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pt-12 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden mb-10 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="b58f63de-29fb-4576-bb30-52d72d7bbc4c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]" data-multiline=""><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Bueno formaliza las locales ;)</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="c75e8271-1b33-461e-9dec-e6e3e2af9185" data-testid="conversation-turn-66" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="d84c1447-ddc2-43bc-8b68-2815a052ea73" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-t-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><h1 data-start="0" data-end="94">Formalización de las <strong data-start="23" data-end="46">MEcuaciones locales</strong> (subfamilios) — teorema, detectores y algoritmo</h1>
<p data-start="96" data-end="411">Voy a formalizar de forma precisa y utilizable la idea de <strong data-start="154" data-end="173">MEcuación local</strong> (ecuación unificadora válida para un <strong data-start="211" data-end="226">subconjunto</strong> de observaciones), dar reglas para <strong data-start="262" data-end="278">encontrarlas</strong>, <strong data-start="280" data-end="297">certificarlas</strong> y <strong data-start="300" data-end="335">describir su dominio de validez</strong>. Incluyo lemas, pruebas esquemáticas y pseudocódigo listo para implementar.</p>
<hr data-start="413" data-end="416">
<h1 data-start="418" data-end="458">1. Definición formal (MEcuación local)</h1>
<p data-start="460" data-end="753">Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{E_1,\dots,E_n\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> un conjunto de observaciones positivas. Sea <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}\to\mathbb{R}^d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8663em; vertical-align: -0.1774em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">&gt;</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1774em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> un <em data-start="575" data-end="588">feature map</em> (p. ej. <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(E)=(\log E,\tfrac12\log E,\; \log E - 2\cdot\tfrac12\log E,\dots)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1901em; vertical-align: -0.345em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span>