04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copiar código</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre!"><span><span>INPUT: S = {E_i}, feature map phi, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">params</span></span><span>: k_max, tau, bootstrap_N, consensus

</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1.</span></span><span> Compute Y = [phi(E_i)] (n x d)
</span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-function">Option <span class="hljs-title">A</span></span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params">si n pequeño</span></span><span>): enumerate all subsets S0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> size&gt;=d_min (costoso)
   </span><span><span class="hljs-function">Option <span class="hljs-title">B</span></span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params">recommended</span></span><span>): cluster Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">into</span></span><span> K </span><span><span class="hljs-title">clusters</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params">K <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.</span></span><span>.k_max) via e.g. agglomerative </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">or</span></span><span> spectral
3. For each cluster C:
     a. Let Yc = rows of Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> C
     b. </span><span><span class="hljs-function">Compute <span class="hljs-title">SVD</span></span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">Yc</span></span><span>) -&gt; singular values S
     c. For r=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1.</span></span><span>.r_max:
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> S[r+</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>]/S[</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>] &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-function">tau <span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title">variance_explained</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">r</span></span><span>) &gt;= </span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>-eta:
              Run bootstrap: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> s=</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1.</span></span><span>.bootstrap_N sample within eps </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> recompute test
              </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">if</span></span><span> fraction_degenerate &gt;= consensus:
                  Accept MEcuation r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> extract Vm = {v1..vr}
                  Validate </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">on</span></span><span> held-</span><span><span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-keyword">out</span></span></span><span> rows </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title">C</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-keyword">or</span></span></span><span> adjacent clusters)
                  Record domain = C
                  Optionally </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">try</span></span><span> to expand domain: greedily </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">add</span></span><span> nearby rows that reduce residual
</span><span><span class="hljs-number">4.</span></span><span> Post-process: </span><span><span class="hljs-function">merge clusters whose MEcuations are <span class="hljs-title">consistent</span></span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params">angle between subspaces small</span></span><span>), </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">remove</span></span><span> trivial singletons.
OUTPUT: list </span><span><span class="hljs-title">of</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-params">MEcuation, domain S0, coefficients, validation scores</span></span><span>)
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="5268" data-end="5369">Parámetros recomendados: <code data-start="5293" data-end="5309">tau=1e-4..1e-6</code> según ruido, <code data-start="5323" data-end="5345">bootstrap_N=200..500</code>, <code data-start="5347" data-end="5368">consensus=0.9..0.99</code>.</p>
<hr data-start="5371" data-end="5374">
<h1 data-start="5376" data-end="5449">6. Certificación del dominio de validez (cómo decir “hasta dónde vale”)</h1>
<p data-start="5451" data-end="5491">Para una MEcuation detectada en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p>
<ul data-start="5493" data-end="6101">
<li data-start="5493" data-end="5689">
<p data-start="5495" data-end="5689"><strong data-start="5495" data-end="5513">Hold-out test:</strong> separar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_0 = T\cup V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∪</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span>. Ajustar la MEcuation en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span>. Calcular residuals en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span>. Aceptar dominio si residuals en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span> están por debajo de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ρ</span></span></span></span> (ej. 3σ del ruido).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5690" data-end="5924">
<p data-start="5692" data-end="5924"><strong data-start="5692" data-end="5722">Expansión por contigüidad:</strong> ordenar observaciones por distancia euclidiana en feature-space a la subespacio; añadir una obs si su residual proyectado &lt; ϵ; repetir hasta estabilizar. Ese conjunto ampliado es el dominio estimado.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5925" data-end="6101">
<p data-start="5927" data-end="6101"><strong data-start="5927" data-end="5960">Test de consistencia modular:</strong> si hay una hipótesis estructural (p. ej. “números cuadrados”), comprobar algebraicamente que la MEcuation implica la estructura y viceversa.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6103" data-end="6106">
<h1 data-start="6108" data-end="6150">7. Ejemplos concretos y su formalización</h1>
<h2 data-start="6152" data-end="6209">Ejemplo A — Subconjunto de cuadrados <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>25</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>49</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>121</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{25,49,121\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord">25</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">49</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">121</span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span></h2>
<ul data-start="6211" data-end="6675">
<li data-start="6211" data-end="6282">
