<hr data-start="178" data-end="181">
<h1 data-start="183" data-end="235">⭐ FRASE CORRECTA (tu idea expresada con precisión)</h1>
<blockquote data-start="237" data-end="429">
<p data-start="239" data-end="429"><strong data-start="239" data-end="429">Si un algoritmo necesita calcular varios logaritmos distintos,<br data-start="303" data-end="306">
y no existe una Magic Equation que los interconecte,<br data-start="360" data-end="363">
entonces cada logaritmo exige su propia iteración obligatoria.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="431" data-end="451">O dicho más técnico:</p>
<blockquote data-start="453" data-end="621">
<p data-start="455" data-end="621"><strong data-start="455" data-end="621">Sin una relación algebraica que reduzca varios <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(E_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span><br data-start="517" data-end="520">
a una sola expresión, el cálculo de cada log es irreductible<br data-start="582" data-end="585">
y no puede eliminarse del bucle.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="623" data-end="733">Eso es <strong data-start="630" data-end="640">verdad</strong>.<br data-start="641" data-end="644">
Y lo demostraste indirectamente al comprobar que no existe MEcuation global en tu modelo.</p>
<hr data-start="735" data-end="738">
<h1 data-start="740" data-end="790">⭐ ¿Por qué es obligatorio? (La explicación fina)</h1>
<p data-start="792" data-end="880">Un algoritmo solo puede <strong data-start="816" data-end="839">ahorrar iteraciones</strong> si existe una identidad matemática tipo:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>MEcuation</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mtext>una&nbsp;sola&nbsp;cosa</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(E_1),\dots,\log(E_k)
\quad\Rightarrow\quad
\text{MEcuation}(\{E_i\}) = \text{una sola cosa}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">MEcuation</span></span><span class="mopen">({</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">})</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">una&nbsp;sola&nbsp;cosa</span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="986" data-end="1022">Si esa ecuación NO existe, entonces:</p>
