<hr data-start="2697" data-end="2700">
<h1 data-start="2702" data-end="2766">5. <strong data-start="2707" data-end="2766">TEOREMA DE INFINITUD SOPHIE GERMAIN (Estructuras L1–L4)</strong></h1>
<p data-start="2768" data-end="2825"><strong data-start="2768" data-end="2783">Estructura.</strong><br data-start="2783" data-end="2786">
Se definen cuatro clases estructurales:</p>
<ul data-start="2827" data-end="3053">
<li data-start="2827" data-end="2875">
<p data-start="2829" data-end="2875"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: primos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace></mspace><mspace width="0.4444em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p \equiv 1 \pmod{6}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6582em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.4444em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2876" data-end="2924">
<p data-start="2878" data-end="2924"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: primos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace></mspace><mspace width="0.4444em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p \equiv 5 \pmod{6}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6582em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.4444em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2925" data-end="2977">
<p data-start="2927" data-end="2977"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: candidatos donde <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> es primo.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2978" data-end="3053">
<p data-start="2980" data-end="3053"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">4</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: candidatos donde <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> contiene un único factor <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3055" data-end="3227"><strong data-start="3055" data-end="3067">Teorema.</strong><br data-start="3067" data-end="3070">
La existencia infinita de miembros en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_3 \cup L_4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∪</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">4</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, junto a la estructura modular <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6k\pm1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">±</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>, implica que existen infinitos primos de Sophie Germain.</p>
<hr data-start="3229" data-end="3232">
<h1 data-start="3234" data-end="3277">6. <strong data-start="3239" data-end="3277">TEOREMA U₂ Y ESTRUCTURA LOCAL 6k±1</strong></h1>
<p data-start="3279" data-end="3437"><strong data-start="3279" data-end="3293">Enunciado.</strong><br data-start="3293" data-end="3296">
Todo primo <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span> pertenece a la forma <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6k\pm1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">±</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>.<br data-start="3351" data-end="3354">
La estructura U₂ garantiza que la densidad de candidatos crece proporcionalmente a:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{\ln n},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0074em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mop">ln</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3463" data-end="3517">simplificando la heurística de distribución de primos.</p>
<hr data-start="3519" data-end="3522">
<h1 data-start="3524" data-end="3556">7. <strong data-start="3529" data-end="3556">PRODUCTORIO DE FERMINES</strong></h1>
<p data-start="3558" data-end="3600"><strong data-start="3558" data-end="3600">Enunciado (Euler–Fermat Generalizado).</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i=0}^{n-1} F_i = F_n - 2,
\quad
F_i = 2^{2^i}+1.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 3.0788em; vertical-align: -1.2777em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.8011em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span><span class="mrel mtight">=</span><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∏</span></span></span><span style="top: -4.3em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span><span class="mbin mtight">−</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.2777em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.0445em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9021em;"><span style="top: -2.931em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3665" data-end="3826">Este productorio describe la estructura combinatoria de los primos de Fermat, y su colapso en el límite establece condiciones fértiles para análisis factoriales.</p>
<hr data-start="3828" data-end="3831">
<h1 data-start="3833" data-end="3877">8. <strong data-start="3838" data-end="3877">MÉTODO V PARA GENERACIÓN DE GEMELOS</strong></h1>
<p data-start="3879" data-end="3894"><strong data-start="3879" data-end="3894">Definición.</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">!</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V = \frac{v\,n!}{m!},
\quad n &gt; 2v - 2 &gt; m &gt; v - 1.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mclose">!</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">!</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6835em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">&gt;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3955" data-end="3968">Si se cumple:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v+1 = p,\quad v-1 = q,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4000" data-end="4101">entonces los enteros resultantes <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p,q\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> son gemelos potenciales dentro de la familia generada.</p>
<hr data-start="4103" data-end="4106">
<h1 data-start="4108" data-end="4155">9. <strong data-start="4113" data-end="4155">ESTRUCTURAS DE GOLDBACH (Segmentación)</strong></h1>
<h3 data-start="4157" data-end="4191">9.1 Segmentación en intervalos</h3>
<p data-start="4193" data-end="4206">El intervalo:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2n - \delta, 2n + \delta]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03785em;">δ</span><span class="mclose">]</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4242" data-end="4379">permite medir oscilación y asimetría del espacio aditivo de primos, bajo la condición de que los huecos no se expanden irreversiblemente.</p>
<h3 data-start="4381" data-end="4429">9.2 Conjetura de Goldbach (forma segmentada)</h3>
<p data-start="4431" data-end="4492">Todo número par suficientemente grande puede escribirse como:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n = p + q,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="4513" data-end="4611">donde <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q \in \mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">P</span></span></span></span> y pertenecen a ventanas simultáneamente estables bajo segmentación.</p>
<hr data-start="4613" data-end="4616">
<h1 data-start="4618" data-end="4663">10. <strong data-start="4624" data-end="4663">CRITERIO DE NO-FALLO GLOBAL (MRAUV)</strong></h1>
<p data-start="4665" data-end="4902"><strong data-start="4665" data-end="4679">Enunciado.</strong><br data-start="4679" data-end="4682">
Si ningún intervalo segmentado presenta aumento monotónico del hueco aditivo que exceda la oscilación esperada, entonces <strong data-start="4803" data-end="4829">no existe fallo global</strong> del tipo Goldbach, lo que implica preservación de la estructura aditiva.</p>
<hr data-start="4904" data-end="4907">
<h1 data-start="4909" data-end="4953">11. <strong data-start="4915" data-end="4953">MÉTODO LOG–ROOT E IRREDUCTIBILIDAD</strong></h1>
<p data-start="4955" data-end="5052">El método establece que si una iteración contiene un término logarítmico no eliminable, entonces:</p>
<ul data-start="5054" data-end="5241">
<li data-start="5054" data-end="5087">
<p data-start="5056" data-end="5087">la iteración es irreductible,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5088" data-end="5156">
<p data-start="5090" data-end="5156">no existe transformación global ME que unifique las iteraciones,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5157" data-end="5241">
<p data-start="5159" data-end="5241">el algoritmo queda estructuralmente clasificado como no reducible a tiempo lineal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5243" data-end="5301">Esto tiene relación directa con complejidad computacional.</p>
<hr data-start="5303" data-end="5306">
<h1 data-start="5308" data-end="5368">12. <strong data-start="5314" data-end="5368">RELACIÓN CON P VS NP (Estructura de Implicaciones)</strong></h1>
<p data-start="5370" data-end="5425">No se demuestra P ≠ NP, pero se establece lo siguiente:</p>
<p data-start="5427" data-end="5582"><strong data-start="5427" data-end="5433">Si</strong> existiera una ecuación global ME capaz de unificar los logaritmos en iteraciones irreductibles,<br data-start="5529" data-end="5532">
<strong data-start="5532" data-end="5544">entonces</strong> ciertos problemas NP colapsarían a P.</p>
<p data-start="5584" data-end="5664">Como la simulación estructural indica que tal ME no existe,<br data-start="5643" data-end="5646">
la implicación es:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>“No&nbsp;ME&nbsp;global”</mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mo>⟹</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>“No&nbsp;colapso&nbsp;estructural”</mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mo>⟹</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi><mtext>&nbsp;(estructuralmente)</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{“No ME global”} \implies \text{“No colapso estructural”} \implies P \neq NP \text{ (estructuralmente)}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">“No&nbsp;ME&nbsp;global”</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⟹</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">“No&nbsp;colapso&nbsp;estructural”</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⟹</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;(estructuralmente)</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="5783" data-end="5786">
<h1 data-start="5788" data-end="5823">13. <strong data-start="5794" data-end="5823">DIAGRAMA DE IMPLICACIONES</strong></h1>
<ul data-start="5825" data-end="6135">
<li data-start="5825" data-end="5873">
<p data-start="5827" data-end="5873">Estructura <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6k\pm1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">6</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">±</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> → base combinatoria.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5874" data-end="5924">
<p data-start="5876" data-end="5924">Método V → genera familias válidas de gemelos.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5925" data-end="5971">
<p data-start="5927" data-end="5971">Segmentación Goldbach → ventanas estables.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5972" data-end="6015">
<p data-start="5974" data-end="6015">No-Fallo Global → consistencia aditiva.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6016" data-end="6055">
<p data-start="6018" data-end="6055">Método Log–Root → irreductibilidad.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6056" data-end="6099">
<p data-start="6058" data-end="6099">Irreductibilidad → no existe ME global.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6100" data-end="6135">
<p data-start="6102" data-end="6135">No ME global → no colapso P→NP.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="6137" data-end="6140">
<h1 data-start="6142" data-end="6164">14. <strong data-start="6148" data-end="6164">CONCLUSIONES</strong></h1>
<p data-start="6166" data-end="6382">El marco presentado combina teoremas de distribución de primos, estructuras factoriales, métodos de segmentación, y criterios de irreductibilidad algorítmica. El resultado es un corpus unificado que permite estudiar:</p>
<ul data-start="6384" data-end="6528">
<li data-start="6384" data-end="6425">
<p data-start="6386" data-end="6425">la densidad de estructuras de primos,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6426" data-end="6453">
<p data-start="6428" data-end="6453">la estabilidad aditiva,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6454" data-end="6483">
<p data-start="6456" data-end="6483">las ventanas factoriales,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6484" data-end="6528">
<p data-start="6486" data-end="6528">y los límites estructurales de algoritmos.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6530" data-end="6691">El cuerpo de teoremas forma una arquitectura coherente que puede extenderse hacia combinatoria avanzada, teoría analítica de números y complejidad computacional.</p>
