<p data-start="276" data-end="362"><strong data-start="276" data-end="304">no puede funcionar jamás</strong> como “Collatz+ por anidación” por un motivo muy concreto:</p>
<hr data-start="364" data-end="367">
<h1 data-start="369" data-end="443">📌 1. EL PROBLEMA: ESTÁS METIENDO UNA OPERACIÓN QUE ROMPE LA ENTERIDAD</h1>
<p data-start="445" data-end="458">Cuando haces:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⋅</mo><mtext>impar</mtext><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>impar</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{2}\cdot\text{impar} + (\text{impar}-2),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.7936em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.1076em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8623em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">impar</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">impar</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="516" data-end="622">aunque el impar sea 3, 5, 7…<br data-start="544" data-end="547">
la expresión <strong data-start="560" data-end="600">no tiene por qué ser divisible por 2</strong> en el siguiente paso.</p>
<p data-start="624" data-end="639">Ejemplo rápido:</p>
<p data-start="641" data-end="646">Sea</p>
<ul data-start="647" data-end="674">
<li data-start="647" data-end="662">
<p data-start="649" data-end="662">número = 20</p>
</li>
<li data-start="663" data-end="674">
<p data-start="665" data-end="674">impar = 5</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="676" data-end="691">Primera capa:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>53.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{20}{2} \cdot 5 + 3 = 10\cdot5 +3 = 53.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0074em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">20</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">10</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">53.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="744" data-end="763">53 es impar ⇒ bien.</p>
<p data-start="765" data-end="800">Pero ahora tu siguiente paso sería:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>53</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{53}{2}\cdot 5 + 3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0074em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">53</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="833" data-end="859"><strong data-start="833" data-end="840">BAM</strong> → ya no es entero.</p>
<p data-start="861" data-end="977">Da igual cuántos “+ impar*k” añadas:<br data-start="897" data-end="900">
si metes un /2 sobre un número impar <strong data-start="937" data-end="976">no hay salvación aritmética posible</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="979" data-end="982">
<h1 data-start="984" data-end="1017">📌 2. LA CORRECCIÓN ESTRUCTURAL</h1>
<p data-start="1019" data-end="1074">Si quieres que TODA tu cadena sea <strong data-start="1053" data-end="1063">entera</strong>, entonces:</p>
<h3 data-start="1076" data-end="1127">✔ Solo existen dos caminos lógicamente válidos:</h3>
<h2 data-start="1129" data-end="1167">(A) Mantienes la división por 2 →</h2>
<p data-start="1168" data-end="1290">Entonces <strong data-start="1177" data-end="1228">la entrada obligatoria debe ser par en ese paso</strong>,<br data-start="1229" data-end="1232">
y DEBES introducir un mecanismo que garantice esa paridad.</p>
<p data-start="1292" data-end="1318">O sea, una regla del tipo:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>↦</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mtext>impar</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto \frac{x\cdot \text{impar} + c}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.522em; vertical-align: -0.011em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↦</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0309em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3449em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">impar</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1370" data-end="1379">requiere:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mtext>impar</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace></mspace><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\cdot \text{impar} + c \equiv 0 \pmod{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4445em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8623em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">impar</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4637em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1430" data-end="1468">Como impar ≡ 1 (mod 2), eso implica:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace></mspace><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow><mspace width="0.3333em"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x + c \equiv 0 \pmod{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4637em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">c</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≡</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mspace allowbreak"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">mod</span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.3333em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1501" data-end="1520">⇒ <strong data-start="1503" data-end="1520">c ≡ x (mod 2)</strong></p>
<p data-start="1522" data-end="1639">Así que tu fórmula debe ADAPTAR el "impar-2" o "+ impar*k" para cumplir esta congruencia.<br data-start="1611" data-end="1614">
Si no, el sistema se cae.</p>
<hr data-start="1641" data-end="1644">
<h2 data-start="1646" data-end="1683">(B) Eliminas la división por 2 →</h2>
<p data-start="1684" data-end="1774">Y lo conviertes en una transformación siempre entera (pero dejaría de ser “Collatz-like”).</p>
<hr data-start="1776" data-end="1779">
<h1 data-start="1781" data-end="1825">📌 3. TU VERSIÓN ANIDADA SE PUEDE ARREGLAR</h1>
