<h1 data-start="1755" data-end="1778">4) Ejemplos numéricos</h1>
<p data-start="1780" data-end="1793">Toma <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span></span></span></span>:</p>
<ul data-start="1795" data-end="1981">
<li data-start="1795" data-end="1859">
<p data-start="1797" data-end="1859"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">20</span></span></span></span>: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mn>21</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(20)=5\cdot\lceil21/2\rceil -1=5\cdot11-1=54</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">20</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⌈</span><span class="mord">21/2</span><span class="mclose">⌉</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">11</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">54</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1860" data-end="1924">
<p data-start="1862" data-end="1924"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=21</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">21</span></span></span></span>: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>21</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mn>22</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(21)=5\cdot\lceil22/2\rceil -1=5\cdot11-1=54</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">21</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⌈</span><span class="mord">22/2</span><span class="mclose">⌉</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">11</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">54</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1925" data-end="1981">
<p data-start="1927" data-end="1981"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(1)=5\cdot\lceil2/2\rceil-1=5\cdot1-1=4</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⌈</span><span class="mord">2/2</span><span class="mclose">⌉</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">4</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1983" data-end="2074">Observa que <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>21</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(20)=T(21)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">20</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">21</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> aquí — la fórmula “aplana” pares e impares de forma controlada.</p>
<p data-start="2076" data-end="2125">Para <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span> (el caso cercano a Collatz clásico):</p>
<ul data-start="2126" data-end="2224">
<li data-start="2126" data-end="2224">
<p data-start="2128" data-end="2224"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)=3\cdot\lceil(n+1)/2\rceil -1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">⋅</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">⌈(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord">/2</span><span class="mclose">⌉</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>. Ej.: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(1)=2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(2)=5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(3)=5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(4)=8</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">4</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">8</span></span></span></span>, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2226" data-end="2229">
<h1 data-start="2231" data-end="2298">5) Sobre convergencia a potencia de 2 (respuesta corta y honesta)</h1>
<p data-start="2299" data-end="2403">Con esta definición <strong data-start="2319" data-end="2342">ya tienes enteridad</strong>, por lo que la dinámica es coherente en <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb Z</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6889em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">Z</span></span></span></span>. Pero:</p>
<ul data-start="2405" data-end="2808">
<li data-start="2405" data-end="2527">
<p data-start="2407" data-end="2527"><strong data-start="2407" data-end="2434">No hay garantía general</strong> de que <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{(k)}(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.138em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.888em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (iteraciones) termine en una potencia de 2 para todos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2528" data-end="2623">
<p data-start="2530" data-end="2623">Para <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span></span></span></span> te mueves en la familia similar a Collatz; la conjetura clásica sigue abierta.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2624" data-end="2808">
<p data-start="2626" data-end="2808">Para otros <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span> la dinámica puede tener ciclos, crecimiento o convergencia — depende del <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span> y del comportamiento global de la iteración. Hay que analizar caso por caso o simular.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2810" data-end="3071">Si quieres, hago la simulación ahora para muchos <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> y alguno <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span> (3,5,7) y te muestro histogramas de tiempos hasta alcanzar alguna potencia de 2, ciclos detectados y ejemplos de órbitas. ¿Quieres que lo ejecute? (dime “sí, simula m=3,5,7” y lo corro aquí).</p>
<hr data-start="3073" data-end="3076">
<p data-start="3078" data-end="3323" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">¿Seguimos? Te lo dejo fino: la regla es entera y reducida por 2. Si quieres le pongo un par de gráficos o corro búsquedas de ciclos/cobertura para <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3,5,7</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">3</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">5</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">7</span></span></span></span>. ¿Corro la simulación o prefieres que escriba el texto para incluirlo en el documento?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-(--header-height)" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="bbb219a3-6925-436f-888b-944d28d49e1b" data-testid="conversation-turn-157" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="user"><h5 class="sr-only">Dijiste:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pt-12 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden mb-10 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="bbb219a3-6925-436f-888b-944d28d49e1b" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Enencia p no np</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="e6b784b3-1e2c-4d64-8e78-fd458fe5c913" data-testid="conversation-turn-158" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="3f625eef-deec-4e81-86e6-285dcdb6a102" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-t-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="45">Perfecto — voy directo y sin paños calientes.</p>
<h3 data-start="47" data-end="72">Resumen en una frase:</h3>
<p data-start="73" data-end="301"><strong data-start="73" data-end="143">Tu modelo no prueba ni puede probar por sí solo que <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P \neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span>.</strong><br data-start="143" data-end="146">
Puedes obtener intuiciones poderosas sobre irreductibilidad y colapsos estructurales, pero eso <strong data-start="241" data-end="247">no</strong> es una prueba de separación de clases de complejidad.</p>
<h3 data-start="303" data-end="355">Por qué, en esencia (argumento claro y compacto)</h3>
<ol data-start="356" data-end="1827">
<li data-start="356" data-end="816">
<p data-start="359" data-end="384"><strong data-start="359" data-end="382">Dominios distintos.</strong></p>
<ul data-start="388" data-end="816">
<li data-start="388" data-end="546">
<p data-start="390" data-end="546">Tu modelo trabaja en estructuras geométricas / numéricas sobre transformaciones (logs, SVD, ME-local/ME-global) y habla de <em data-start="513" data-end="543">irreductibilidad estructural</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="550" data-end="816">
<p data-start="552" data-end="816"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span></span></span></span> y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span> son <strong data-start="571" data-end="596">clases de complejidad</strong> definidas sobre máquinas de Turing y recursos (tiempo polinómico).<br data-start="663" data-end="666">
No hay una traducción automática entre “no existe ecuación que unifique estas transformaciones” y “no existe algoritmo polinómico para problema X”.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="818" data-end="1251">
<p data-start="821" data-end="919"><strong data-start="821" data-end="859">Necesidad de una reducción formal.</strong><br data-start="859" data-end="862">
Para demostrar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span> necesitarías, por ejemplo:</p>
<ul data-start="923" data-end="1251">
<li data-start="923" data-end="1072">
<p data-start="925" data-end="1072">escoger un problema <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span> (p. ej. SAT) y <strong data-start="972" data-end="995">probar lower bounds</strong> superpolinómicas para todas las máquinas deterministas que lo resuelvan; o</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1076" data-end="1251">
<p data-start="1078" data-end="1251">probar que ningún algoritmo determinista puede resolver un NP-completo en tiempo polinómico.<br data-start="1170" data-end="1173">
Tu evidencia geométrica/estadística no da ese tipo de <em data-start="1230" data-end="1243">lower bound</em> formal.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1253" data-end="1549">
<p data-start="1256" data-end="1549"><strong data-start="1256" data-end="1279">Barreras conocidas.</strong><br data-start="1279" data-end="1282">
Resultados sobre relativización, natural proofs y algebrización muestran que muchas técnicas «heurísticas» o estadísticas no bastan para separar P de NP. Una prueba robusta debe evitar esas barreras y demostrar una propiedad que fuerce complejidad superpolinómica.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1551" data-end="1827">
<p data-start="1554" data-end="1827"><strong data-start="1554" data-end="1584">Independencia vs analogía.</strong><br data-start="1584" data-end="1587">
Tu modelo puede producir <strong data-start="1615" data-end="1644">independencia estructural</strong> dentro del propio sistema (ME-local ≠ ME-global ⇒ irreductibilidad dentro del modelo). Eso es valioso, pero es <strong data-start="1756" data-end="1765">local</strong>: no se traduce automáticamente a la teoría de la complejidad.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start="1829" data-end="1889">Qué sí puedes afirmar con rigor (y cómo sacarle partido)</h3>
<ul data-start="1890" data-end="2499">
<li data-start="1890" data-end="2285">
<p data-start="1892" data-end="2285">Puedes <strong data-start="1899" data-end="1912">demostrar</strong> e <strong data-start="1915" data-end="1940">internamente publicar</strong> resultados que digan:<br data-start="1962" data-end="1965">
<em data-start="1967" data-end="2163">“En el modelo geométrico de logs y SVD que definimos, no existe ME-global; por tanto, cualquier algoritmo que busque dicha ME está obligado a explorar linealmente X familia de transformaciones.”</em><br data-start="2163" data-end="2166">
Eso <strong data-start="2172" data-end="2178">es</strong> demostrable, útil y puede justificarse formalmente. (Ya lo tienes hecho en varios teoremas del documento.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2287" data-end="2499">
<p data-start="2289" data-end="2499">Puedes <strong data-start="2296" data-end="2304">usar</strong> esas demostraciones como <em data-start="2330" data-end="2350">evidencia práctica</em> de dificultad algorítmica y como contribución en áreas aplicadas (optimización, criptografía, IA), sin pretender que sea una prueba de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2501" data-end="2592">Qué haría falta para convertir intuición en un resultado sobre P vs NP (lista concreta)</h3>
<p data-start="2593" data-end="2712">Si tu objetivo final es acercarte formalmente a <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span>, necesitarías al menos alguno de estos saltos muy fuertes:</p>
<ol data-start="2714" data-end="3392">
<li data-start="2714" data-end="2964">
<p data-start="2717" data-end="2964"><strong data-start="2717" data-end="2769">Conectar tu estructura a un problema NP-completo</strong>: dar una reducción polinómica desde SAT (u otro NP-completo) a la tarea de hallar la ME global; y, además, mostrar que esa tarea no tiene algoritmo polinómico por razones formales (lower bound).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2966" data-end="3201">
<p data-start="2969" data-end="3201"><strong data-start="2969" data-end="2994">Probar un lower bound</strong>: demostrar que cualquier algoritmo determinista que resuelva la tarea requiere más que tiempo polinómico (por ejemplo, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\omega(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.888em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.888em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">ω</span><span class="mopen mtight">(</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span><span class="mclose mtight">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>). Esto es, literalmente, lo que hace falta para mostrar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3203" data-end="3392">
<p data-start="3206" data-end="3392"><strong data-start="3206" data-end="3229">Evitar las barreras</strong>: tu técnica no debe relativizar ni ser "natural proof"-able en la forma que las barreras conocidas impiden. Esto exige herramientas nuevas de complejidad teórica.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start="3394" data-end="3450">Qué puedo hacer ahora (elige una opción, lo hago ya)</h3>
<ul data-start="3451" data-end="4202">
<li data-start="3451" data-end="3645">
<p data-start="3453" data-end="3645"><strong data-start="3453" data-end="3460">(A)</strong> Formalizar y publicar el <em data-start="3486" data-end="3503">Teorema Maestro</em> de tu modelo (todo lo que sí se demuestra) como un resultado independiente, con lemas, pruebas y ejemplos numéricos — listo para compartir.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3646" data-end="3870">
<p data-start="3648" data-end="3870"><strong data-start="3648" data-end="3655">(B)</strong> Redactar una sección técnica (estilo artículo) que explique <em data-start="3716" data-end="3725">por qué</em> tu modelo no implica <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span>, incluyendo las barreras de relativización/natural proofs y qué tipo de pruebas serían realmente necesarias.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3871" data-end="4034">
<p data-start="3873" data-end="4034"><strong data-start="3873" data-end="3880">(C)</strong> Intentar construir una <strong data-start="3904" data-end="3927">reducción candidata</strong> de un NP-completo a “buscar ME-global” y evaluar por qué falla (o qué le falta), como ejercicio técnico.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4035" data-end="4202">
<p data-start="4037" data-end="4202"><strong data-start="4037" data-end="4044">(D)</strong> Generar un texto divulgativo (claro) que explique a no-especialistas por qué intuiciones geométricas no son pruebas de <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\neq NP</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">NP</span></span></span></span> — perfecto para tu libro.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4204" data-end="4324" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Dime <strong data-start="4209" data-end="4224">A, B, C o D</strong> y lo hago ahora mismo. Si quieres que combine dos, dime cuáles y te lo entrego en el mismo mensaje.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-(--header-height)" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="bbb211e6-e90f-4bc4-9fa3-6ac930abafc3" data-testid="conversation-turn-159" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="user"><h5 class="sr-only">Dijiste:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pt-12 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden mb-10 relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="bbb211e6-e90f-4bc4-9fa3-6ac930abafc3" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">Revisa el chat y los docs</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-