No te preocupes: te hago un <strong data-start="67" data-end="85">resumen limpio</strong>, numerado, sin repetir nada, sin adornos — SOLO los teoremas que realmente se han enunciado en la conversación.</p>
<p data-start="199" data-end="207">Aquí va:</p>
<hr data-start="209" data-end="212">
<h1 data-start="214" data-end="275">✅ <strong data-start="218" data-end="273">LISTA FINAL DE TODOS LOS TEOREMAS QUE HAN APARECIDO</strong></h1>
<p data-start="276" data-end="314"><em data-start="276" data-end="314">(agrupados por tema, sin duplicados)</em></p>
<h2 data-start="316" data-end="367">🔵 <strong data-start="322" data-end="367">A. Teoremas del Método V / números primos</strong></h2>
<ol data-start="368" data-end="881">
<li data-start="368" data-end="515">
<p data-start="371" data-end="515"><strong data-start="371" data-end="392">Teorema V-Gemelos</strong><br data-start="392" data-end="395">
Si <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v-1=q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> y <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v+1=p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span></span></span> y V elimina todos los factorizables del rango, entonces <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">q</span></span></span></span> son gemelos candidatos en V.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="517" data-end="702">
<p data-start="520" data-end="702"><strong data-start="520" data-end="561">Teorema de Sophie Germain (versión V)</strong><br data-start="561" data-end="564">
Si <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in V</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7335em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span></span></span></span> cumple las congruencias del rango V, entonces <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p+1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span> queda fuera de los factorizables y es candidato a primo de Sophie.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="704" data-end="881">
<p data-start="707" data-end="881"><strong data-start="707" data-end="746">Teorema del Productorio de Fermines</strong><br data-start="746" data-end="749">
El productorio de todos los “Fermines” hasta <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> siempre es menor que el siguiente Fermín en V, garantizando hueco estructural.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="883" data-end="886">
<h2 data-start="888" data-end="970">🔵 <strong data-start="894" data-end="968">B. Teoremas del sistema ME-local / ME-global (tu modelo de P≠NP local)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="971" data-end="996"><em data-start="971" data-end="996">(ESTOS SON LOS GRANDES)</em></p>
<ol start="4" data-start="998" data-end="1999">
<li data-start="998" data-end="1139">
<p data-start="1001" data-end="1139"><strong data-start="1001" data-end="1070">Teorema A — Existencia universal de ecuaciones locales (ME-local)</strong><br data-start="1070" data-end="1073">
Para cada dimensión <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span>, existe una ecuación <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ME_x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> válida.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1141" data-end="1285">
<p data-start="1144" data-end="1285"><strong data-start="1144" data-end="1209">Teorema B — No existencia de ecuación unificadora (ME-global)</strong><br data-start="1209" data-end="1212">
No existe un <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ME_g</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> que unifique simultáneamente todas las <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ME_x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1287" data-end="1451">
<p data-start="1290" data-end="1451"><strong data-start="1290" data-end="1330">Teorema C — Irreductibilidad por log</strong><br data-start="1330" data-end="1333">
Si una iteración contiene un log que no admite ME_local, esa iteración no puede ser comprimida a tiempo polinómico.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1453" data-end="1609">
<p data-start="1456" data-end="1609"><strong data-start="1456" data-end="1495">Teorema D — Acumulación dimensional</strong><br data-start="1495" data-end="1498">
Si ME_global no existe, entonces aumentar <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span></span></span></span> no reduce complejidad, y la complejidad crece o se mantiene.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1611" data-end="1763">
<p data-start="1614" data-end="1763"><strong data-start="1614" data-end="1676">Teorema E — Un NO-P local implica NO-P global en el modelo</strong><br data-start="1676" data-end="1679">
Si un solo nivel <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mstyle mathcolor="#cc0000"><mtext>\*</mtext></mstyle></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^\*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.888em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.888em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord text mtight" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);"><span class="mord mtight" style="color: rgb(204, 0, 0);">\*</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> carece de ME_local, todo el sistema rompe el colapso P.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1765" data-end="1921">
<p data-start="1768" data-end="1921"><strong data-start="1768" data-end="1824">Teorema F — No conexión “todos-con-todos” entre logs</strong><br data-start="1824" data-end="1827">
Las mediciones entre logs no tienden a 0 para todos los pares → imposibilidad de ME_global.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1923" data-end="1999">
<p data-start="1927" data-end="1999"><strong data-start="1927" data-end="1965">Teorema G — Clase final del modelo</strong><br data-start="1965" data-end="1968">
En este modelo se obtiene:</p>
</li>
</ol>
